# The alternate (callback) interface: rl_callback_handler_install +
# rl_callback_read_char driven by the driver's select loop.
tags: callback

=== single-line
--- script
callback "cb> "
--- keys
hello\r

=== multiple-lines-with-history
--- script
callback "cb> " 3 addhist
history_dump
--- keys
one\rtwo\r\C-p\C-p<dump>\r

=== eof-ends-loop
--- script
callback "cb> " all
--- keys
abc\r

=== manual-read-char
--- script
callback_install "m> "
callback_read_char 3
dump
callback_read_char
rl_callback_handler_remove
--- keys
ab\r

=== state-flags-in-callback
--- script
callback "cb> "
--- keys
a<dumpfull>\r

=== isearch-in-callback
tags: isearch
--- script
add_history "make test"
add_history "ls"
callback "cb> "
--- keys
\C-rmak<snap>\r

=== sigint-in-callback
--- script
def onint
dump
rl_free_line_state
rl_callback_sigcleanup
rl_cleanup_after_signal
end
onsig onint
callback "cb> " 2
--- keys
abc\C-cdef\r

=== vi-mode-callback
--- inputrc
set editing-mode vi
set keyseq-timeout 50
--- script
callback "cb> "
--- keys
abc\e<pause>0x<dump>\r

=== completion-in-callback
tags: complete
--- script
complete_words callback callable
set rl_attempted_completion_function words
callback "cb> "
--- keys
cal\t\t<snap>\r

=== prompt-redisplay-after-line
--- script
callback "cb> " 2
--- keys
first\r<snap>second\r

=== handler-remove-inside
--- script
callback_install "x> "
callback_read_char 2
rl_callback_handler_remove
get rl_readline_state
--- keys
q\r
